// Stock SIMH Type 630 TCC helper.
//
// Stock SIMH models the original one-byte-per-line DCS buffer.  A bare TCC
// schedules transmission and returns before that byte has necessarily left;
// another TCC can therefore overwrite the same buffer.  DCS2 does not have
// that source-level constraint.
//
// Under SIMH_COMPAT, simhdcsdefs.ah maps each source-level TCC to this local
// JDA helper.  One copy is assembled in every ZMachine bank that emits TCC.
// The helper waits for the stock DCS scanner flag, consumes the transmit
// completion with RCC (rchr), restores the caller's AC, and leaves IO holding
// the transmitted byte as the native IOT usefully does.

simhtcc, 0
local rtn, wait
     dap rtn
     // IO still holds the outgoing byte supplied by the caller.
     iot 5022
wait,
     cli
     cks
     lai
     and [SIMH_DCS_READY
     sza i
     jmp wait
     cli
     rchr
     lac simhtcc
rtn, jmp .
endloc
